        "question_type": "single_choice",
        "question_title": "For what values of \\(a\\) does the quadratic equation \\(x^2-2(a+1)x+a^2+3=0\\) have both roots greater than \\(1\\)?",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "Putting \\(x=y+1\\) gives \\(y^2-2ay+(a-1)^2+1=0\\). Its discriminant is \\(8(a-1)\\), while the sum and product of the roots are positive for \\(a\\ge1\\). Hence both roots \\(y\\), and therefore both roots \\(x\\), are positive relative to \\(1\\) exactly when \\(a\\ge1\\).",
        "question_audio": null,
        "time_limit_seconds": 30,
